# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Copy this file to .env.local and fill in the value.
#
#   cp .env.local.example .env.local
#
# .env.local is gitignored. This example file is not — never put real values
# here.
#
# The variable is NEXT_PUBLIC_, meaning it is inlined into the static build and
# visible in page source. That is correct here: a Formspree form ID is a public
# endpoint by design. Do NOT add any secret with a NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix.
#
# Because it is baked in at build time, changing it requires a rebuild and
# redeploy — restarting the dev server is not enough. The same value must also
# be set on the Vercel project (Settings → Environment Variables), because
# Vercel builds remotely and never reads this file.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Formspree form ID — the part after /f/ in your form's endpoint URL.
# Find it at https://formspree.io → your form → Integration → the endpoint
# reads https://formspree.io/f/xxxxxxxx — copy just the xxxxxxxx.
# Without this, the contact form renders disabled with a visible setup notice
# rather than silently swallowing leads.
NEXT_PUBLIC_FORMSPREE_ID=
